From b35bbef24cf278472047cbfe149a9e2dd64bc5bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:15:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clocksource/drivers/timer-ti-dm: suspend runtime-active
 timers for system sleep

A timer that is runtime active when system suspend starts stays active:
the PM core holds a runtime PM reference across system sleep, so even a
user that stops the timer in its own suspend callback (pwm-omap-dmtimer
via pwm-backlight) doesn't get it runtime suspended. ti-sysc then idles
the module in the noirq phase, and the CPU PM notifier, which still sees
timer->enabled, saves the context of a module without clocks. On a
Samsung Galaxy Tab 2 10.1 (backlight PWM on timer10) every suspend to
RAM with the backlight on dies with

  Unhandled fault: imprecise external abort (0x1406)
  PC is at omap_timer_save_context+0x6c/0x130
   omap_timer_context_notifier from notifier_call_chain
   ...
   cpu_pm_notify_robust from syscore_suspend

Force the timers into runtime suspend in the late system sleep phase,
which saves their context and clears timer->enabled before the module
is idled, and resume them again afterwards.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clocksource/timer-ti-dm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clocksource/timer-ti-dm.c b/drivers/clocksource/timer-ti-dm.c
index 6787acac9a43..56e443bc63d6 100644
--- a/drivers/clocksource/timer-ti-dm.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/timer-ti-dm.c
@@ -1198,6 +1198,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused omap_dm_timer_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops omap_dm_timer_pm_ops = {
+	SET_LATE_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend,
+				     pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(omap_dm_timer_runtime_suspend,
 			   omap_dm_timer_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
